+## What the update contains
+
+The update has fixed sections: TL;DR, a KPI table, a default-alive check, highlights,
+lowlights, product, team and asks. The model writes the prose. Two parts are computed in
+code from confirmed facts, so the model never writes their numbers:
+
+- **KPI table.** ARR, paying teams, NRR, demos, net burn, cash and runway, with September,
+  October and the change.
+- **Default alive?** Paul Graham's
+  [default alive or default dead](https://paulgraham.com/aord.html) test. If costs stay
+  flat and ARR keeps growing at this month's rate, does revenue cover costs before the
+  cash runs out? It also gives the growth rate where the answer flips. On the demo data:
+  default alive, break-even in 13 months with €1.83M left, and default dead below about
+  8.6% monthly growth.
 
